# Auto-push after changes

When the user asks for fixes, features, or implementation work:

1. After changes are complete and verified (lint/syntax OK), **commit and push** without waiting to be asked.
2. Push **every repo** that was modified (e.g. Website-dominues, Game-dominues, backend).
3. Use clear commit messages focused on the "why".
4. Do **not** push secrets (`.env`, credentials).
5. Do **not** force-push to main/master.
6. Report the commit hash(es) and confirm push succeeded.

Only skip push if the user explicitly says not to push, or if there are no changes to commit.
